  "about": "Reference pronunciations for biblical and Church names, as used in English church reading (lector guides; the owner's audio Bible where checked). ipa is in Kokoro's own phoneme notation (misaki, US English): ˈ primary stress before the stressed vowel, ˌ secondary, A = 'ay', I = 'eye', O = 'oh', ɹ = r, ʤ = j. say is a plain respelling for people. The pronunciation-audit workflow compares each entry with how Kokoro already says the name; only mismatches are auditioned, and only approved ones become rules. Everyday names Kokoro's dictionary already knows (John, Paul, Egypt...) are deliberately left out. Add a name here to have it checked on the next audit.",
